# Encrypted broker credential material (Fernet-encrypted JSON per elements_v2.md §1.2)
*credentials*.json
*creds*.json

# Non-Plane artifacts only (logs/ per directory_structure.md) — never commit these anyway
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# pg_dump staging (Backblaze pipeline) — binary/compressed backup artifacts only.
# databases/schema/ (extracted DDL — the source-of-truth schema artifacts) IS tracked;
# directory_structure.md explicitly scopes "auxiliary DB files" into this directory,
# and a blanket databases/* rule silently defeated that. Never the PG cluster itself
# (that lives at the OS-default location per elements_v2.md, outside ~/nix entirely).
databases/*.dump
databases/*.sql.gz
databases/*.tar
databases/backups/

# Node-identity / runtime state (state/ — hardware UUID, credential JSON). Not for a
# public repo: the hardware UUID is machine-fingerprinting info, not a secret exactly,
# but not something to publish either. credentials.json is already covered above by
# *credentials*.json but state/ is excluded wholesale for defense in depth.
state/

# Env / master-password material
*.env
.env
*master_password*
*master-password*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
# testmon's SQLite database and its WAL/shared-memory sidecars. The bare name alone
# did NOT cover the sidecars, and ARC 016 caught `.testmondata-shm` / `.testmondata-wal`
# being staged by a `git add -A`. Committing them would put a machine-local, constantly
# rewritten binary cache into history and make every commit conflict on it.
.testmondata
.testmondata-shm
.testmondata-wal

# macOS cruft (not part of the tracked tree)
.DS_Store
._*

# graphify working output (not part of this arc's scope)
graphify-out/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Local Claude Code launcher (operator convenience, never published)
scripts/cl.sh

# Inbound CODE drafts delivered into downloads/ by claude.ai. The arc briefs
# (downloads/arc_*.md) ARE tracked — they are the design authority for an arc and
# history should hold them. The .py drafts are NOT: every one of them has since been
# landed under scripts/ and evolved well past the delivered version (ARC 016 measured
# broker_seam 626 -> 790 lines, simulate 258 -> 525, test_broker_order 489 -> 1270).
# Committing them would put a second, stale copy of live code in the tree — a
# derive-never-restate violation (CLAUDE.md directive 3) that the gate would then lint
# as if it were real, and that a future reader could mistake for the implementation.
# The landed file under scripts/ is the single source of truth.
downloads/*.py
